;; The module termios (queue 220; Modules/termios.c and Modules/clinic/termios.c.h of CPython 3.14.10, PSF License
;; Agreement): tcgetattr, tcsetattr, tcsendbreak, tcdrain, tcflush, tcflow, tcgetwinsize and tcsetwinsize over Linux's
;; tty ioctls as musl's termios functions make them (src/termios/*.c: tcgetattr is TCGETS, tcsetattr TCSETS+when,
;; tcsendbreak TCSBRK 0, tcdrain TCSBRK 1, tcflush TCFLSH, tcflow TCXONC; cfgetospeed is c_cflag&CBAUD, cfsetospeed
;; sets it), the struct's bytes passed by their address (reflect's Pointer, as mmap's msync: no unsafe), and the
;; constants of musl's headers on Linux (amd64 and arm64 alike: asm-generic's termbits and ioctls), in termios.c's
;; order. os.openpty (posixmodule.c over musl's openpty) is here too: it is what tty and termios' tests open.
;;
;; musl's struct termios: c_iflag, c_oflag, c_cflag, c_lflag (4 bytes each), c_line, c_cc[NCCS=32], the speeds; the
;; kernel's TCGETS fills the first 36 bytes (its c_cc has 19), so c_cc[19:] stay zero (CPython's memset for Alpine).

